/Title (Three quick checks worth internalizing: not every dataset has all three measures defined \(a purely nominal dataset has no mean\); in a normal \(symmetric, bell-shaped\) distribution the mean, median and mode coincide; and among the three, the mean and median are always single, unique values, while the mode may be non-unique \(multimodal\) or, for continuous data with no repeated values, may not exist in a useful sense. )
