/Title (2.4 Interquartile Range \(IQR\) )
/Dest [20 0 R /XYZ 72.558594 663.85791 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 94 0 R
/Prev 619 0 R
/Next 623 0 R
>>
endobj
622 0 obj
<<
/Title (A common rule of thumb flags any value more than 1.5 times the IQR above Q3 or below Q1 as a suspected outlier. Why 1.5 and not 1 or 3? For normally distributed data, 1.5 times IQR corresponds to roughly plus or minus 2.7 standard deviations from the mean, which flags only about 0.7% of points as outliers - a threshold tight enough to be useful but loose enough to avoid flagging ordinary variation. A stricter multiplier, like 1, would flag far too many ordinary points; a looser one, like 3, would miss real outliers. )
/Dest [20 0 R /XYZ 72.187988 542.24316 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 97 0 R
/Prev 624 0 R
/Next 620 0 R
>>
endobj
623 0 obj
<<
/Title (The IQR is the distance between the first and third quartiles - the range covered by the middle half of the data. )
/Dest [20 0 R /XYZ 72.080566 632.41064 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 95 0 R
/Prev 621 0 R
